{"name":"Hepatica","hex":"#fbe5ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hepatica","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The liverworts, taxonomically treated either as\nA taxonomic section within the family Ranunculaceae – Anemone sect. Hepatica. or\nA taxonomic genus within the family Ranunculaceae.","A taxonomic section within the family Ranunculaceae – Anemone sect. Hepatica. or"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hepatica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hepatica","blocks":[{"text":"Hepatica is a genus of herbaceous perennials in the buttercup family, native to central and northern Europe, Asia and eastern North America. Some botanists include Hepatica within a wider interpretation of Anemone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Hepatica_nobilis_plant.JPG/330px-Hepatica_nobilis_plant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hepatica","wikidata":"Q157505"},{"title":"Hepatica (moth)","blocks":[{"text":"Hepatica  is a genus of moths of the family Erebidae. The genus was described by Staudinger in 1892."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hepatica_(moth)","wikidata":"Q5731690"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Hepatica_transsylvanica.jpg/500px-Hepatica_transsylvanica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Hepatica_transsylvanica.jpg/1280px-Hepatica_transsylvanica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Hepatica_transsylvanica.jpg/500px-Hepatica_transsylvanica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hepatica transsilvanica","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHepatica_transsylvanica.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe